By removing the `IRQF_TRIGGER_HIGH` flag and only using `IRQF_ONESHOT`, the code now respects the trigger types defined by the firmware. This ensures that the interrupt mapping aligns correctly with the firmware expectations, preventing the type mismatch errors during wakeup interrupt requests.


